      Q("workup", "Which EKG findings support pulmonic stenosis?", ["RV hypertrophy and right axis deviation", "LVH and left axis deviation", "LA enlargement and AF", "Low voltage"], 0, "PS: EKG shows RV hypertrophy and right axis deviation; echo is the test of choice."),
      Q("treatment", "When is pulmonic valve replacement indicated for pulmonic stenosis?", ["Severe cases or when surgical correction of congenital heart disease is indicated", "All mild cases at diagnosis", "Only after rheumatic fever", "Never; it is managed medically"], 0, "PS is monitored with serial echo (often in a congenital heart disease clinic); replace in severe cases or with congenital heart surgery.")
